  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday Night through Saturday)\nIssued at 1006 PM CST Sat Nov 21 2026\n\nCold front will continue to move across southeast Ok and western\nAR early Sunday morning with strong and gusty northwest winds\nbringing notably cooler air. With the late night and early \nmorning timing of the front passage, temps will follow an non-\ntypical diurnal trend, and in some areas not warm much above the \nmorning readings. This will be especially true if cloud cover is \nmore stubborn to erode as suggested by more high-res guidance. \n\nA cooler surface high from Canada will continue to settle over \nthe Central CONUS early next week and result in a stretch of \nbelow normal temps. Most of the region will see a hard freeze on \nmore than one night during the middle part of the week, with some \nupper teens likely for parts of northwest AR and far northeast OK.\n\nNext upper wave is forecast to move from the high plains and track\nESE into AR/LA late Tue and Wed. Southern track and lack of \navailable moisture should keep the forecast area dry. Rest of the\nThanksgiving week looks dry as well, with a slow warm into next \nweekend.",
